abstract: Fu ying xin shuo (婦嬰新說), written by Benjamin Hobson with Guan mao cai and catalogued as an 1858 Shanghai edition issued by Ren ji yi guan, discusses female reproductive anatomy, pregnancy, childbirth, childhood illness and historical remedies, with medical illustrations. The dataset supports preliminary searching, location and image checking for medical history, translation and illustration research. Based on Bodleian Libraries, University of Oxford, Sinica 1792, this edition provides a source-faithful transcription of 128 faces and a bibliographical and circulation-history guide for the nine faces p129–137, without that chapter’s operational text. JSON, TXT and TEI preserve source characters, printed punctuation, small notes and diagram labels, with links to the original. Version 0.2.0 uses independent AI reading comparison followed by nonblind, face-by-face source adjudication; no human full-text collation has been performed, and uncertainties are marked.
